# VRK160 EDF (Yocto) build configuration.
#
# Sourced by sdbuild/scripts/build_edf_boot.sh. Names the Yocto machine
# bitbake targets and selects the build mode.
#
# EDF_MODE=custom -> the Yocto machine is generated from the PYNQ golden XSA
# (sdtgen + gen-machine-conf), so BOOT.BIN loads the PYNQ golden as the Versal
# segmented static/parent design. The runtime base overlay (base.pdi) is a
# segmented child of that same golden, so its parent image ID matches at load
# time. EDF_BOOT_MACHINE MUST NOT collide with an upstream machine name in
# meta-amd-adaptive-socs-bsp (e.g. versal-vrk160-sdt-seg, if one exists);
# otherwise bitbake resolves the upstream machine and ignores the
# golden-derived config. The pynq- prefix keeps the name unique.
#
# EDF_BOARD_DTS is intentionally omitted: VRK160 is a Versal Gen 2 (VR
# series, ES1 silicon) board and there is no confirmed board DTS name for it
# in meta-amd-adaptive-socs-bsp under the amd-edf-rel-v25.11.1 manifest.
# Omitting it falls back to the generic SoC device tree, with everything
# board-specific supplied via edf_bsp/board.dtsi. If a real
# "versal-vrk160-*" board DTS turns up in that layer, set it here instead.

EDF_MANIFEST_TAG=amd-edf-rel-v25.11.1
EDF_MODE=custom
EDF_BOOT_MACHINE=versal-vrk160-pynq-seg
EDF_LINUX_MACHINE=amd-cortexa72-common
BSP_XSA_PATH=golden/golden.xsa
